  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.0: the rest of the Messaging API plus LIFF. New: webhook endpoint get / set / test, account link tokens, image preview and video transcoding status, a LIFF server client (ILineLiffClient, registered with AddLineLiff, using the LINE Login channel token through its own named HttpClient), message delivery counts, per-send and per-unit engagement insight, custom aggregation units on push / multicast / broadcast / narrowcast, rich menu batch operations (link, unlink, unlink all) with validation and progress, and PushManyAsync / MulticastManyAsync that split an oversized send into batches of 5 messages and 500 recipients, in order, stopping at the first failure and deriving a stable RetryKey per batch. Webhook events and messages are typed further (join, leave, beacon, unsend, account link, membership, emoji, mention, image set, quoted message, mark-as-read token); outgoing text can carry emoji and a new textV2 message supports mentions and emoji by substitution. Local validation now covers text and alt text length, media URLs, action labels, postback data, uri schemes, colours, textV2 substitution and every rich menu area action, failing with line.validation.invalid_message or invalid_action before anything is sent. Serialising a concrete message or action type directly now produces the same JSON as serialising it as LineMessage or LineAction. New error codes: invalid_message, invalid_action, invalid_webhook_endpoint, invalid_liff_app, invalid_date_range, invalid_aggregation_unit, invalid_rich_menu_batch and no_recipients; existing codes and categories are unchanged. See https://github.com/ozakboy/Ozakboy.Line/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
